      "transports": [
        "tcp-server"
      ],
      "source": "Jammu Getein MAGICL 6000i. Item ids and analyzer units supplied by the lab as a spreadsheet (SEP 2026, 17 assays). Same getein HL7 v2.3.1 / MLLP dialect as the Delhi and Rohtak 6000i units, so no driver work was needed. Every Noble target was read back from what Jammu itself registers (1200 recent samples scanned) rather than copied from another site.",
      "mappingsSummary": {
        "total": 17,
        "mapped": 17,
        "unmapped": 0
      },
      "_mappingNotes": [
        "Analyte key is the MAGICL numeric item id from OBX-3, with the friendly name in OBX-4. These match the Delhi/Rohtak 6000i numbering (TSH=18, T3=19, T4=20, FT3=21, FT4=22) — NOT the Rohtak 6200, which uses those ids + 1000.",
